n actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`","anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift 6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mode","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0"},{"type":"text","text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nonisolated init"},{"type":"text","text":" does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”","anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var flag = false"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var flag: Bool = false"},{"type":"text","text":". The same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applies to combined declarations: split "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var a, b: Int"},{"text":" into separate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declarations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Keychain writes fail with OSStatus −34018 (`errSecMissingEntitlement`)","anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An unsigned local or CI build is using ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"text":" without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"provisioning profile. This is a signing condition, not a prompt or a bug — the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data-protection keychain never prompts. Ship provisioning-profile-signed builds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessGroup: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; for unsigned local\/CI builds add a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"team-prefixed ","type":"text"},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entitlement. Details in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Edits disappear after a sync tick or an async load","anchor":"Edits-disappear-after-a-sync-tick-or-an-async-load"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Symptom: a keystroke, a toggle, or a whole entity vanishes — intermittently,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"usually while something is loading or syncing, and never reproducibly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The cause is almost always a hand-rolled bridge from ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" work into the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps state in an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" observer tree and converts to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-type snapshot on the way in and out (“pack” and “unpack”). If you pack a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" something, and then unpack it, everything dispatched during","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is silently overwritten:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var snapshot = AppState(observer: store.observer)   \/\/ ← packed BEFORE the await","await loadEverything(into: &snapshot)               \/\/ ← dispatches land here…","AppState.apply(snapshot, to: store.observer)        \/\/ ← …and are discarded here"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" across a suspension point is the tell. The window is only as wide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is why it presents as a rare glitch rather than a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reproducible bug.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)"},{"text":" instead. It runs the async work with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"access to state, then packs a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"fresh"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" snapshot, merges, and unpacks in a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"step with no suspension point in between — so no dispatch can interleave:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["await store.mutate {","    try await api.fetchItems()          \/\/ no state in scope; nothing to stale","} merging: { items, state in","    state.items.merge(from: EntityStore(items)) { _, _ in false }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The persistence stack’s own async entry points already work this way — use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"persistence.rehydrate(into: store)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sync.setSyncEnabled(_:into: store)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a snapshot you manage yourself. (","type":"text"},{"code":"hydrate(into: &state)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the exception,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and safe: it runs at launch, before the store exists.)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Contributors: the lint plugin doesn’t run \/ dev tooling is missing","anchor":"Contributors-the-lint-plugin-doesnt-run--dev-tooling-is-missing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dev tooling (the Persnoop linter, the DocC plugin) is gated behind a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gitignored ","type":"text"},{"code":".dev-tooling","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sentinel file so it never leaks into consumers’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dependency graphs. Create it at the package root — and if the package was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already built without it, run ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift package purge-cache","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so SwiftPM re-reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the manifest. See the repository’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CONTRIBUTING.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"A `@Persisted` app crashes only in Release","anchor":"A-Persisted-app-crashes-only-in-Release"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the crash is in fetching, make sure you’re on ≥ 1.3.0: generic","type":"text"}